PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Split in round 0: 8 colleagues pick A (most detailed), 4 pick E, 2 pick D, 1 picks B. Core tests from NI 45-106 (Jan 2021): individuals via income (>200k solo/>300k spousal, 2 prior yrs + expectation), net financial assets (≥1M), or net assets (≥5M); entities via own net assets ≥5M on FS or all direct/indirect owners themselves AIs. 

Key claims preserved: A fails because GP holding co lacks proven AI status (gifts alone insufficient for its own net-asset test or owner chain); E fails because Alex/Bob individually miss thresholds and corp net assets cannot be confirmed ≥5M (unknown investment-property values). Counter-claims: E's GIC-liability math yields 5.2M (meets entity test); A's LPs + GP all qualify individually so LP satisfies "all owners" route; D fails only on James's 285k combined income leaving one non-AI shareholder. 

Unresolved: whether GP corp's 6M gifted cash counts as its own net assets for entity test, and whether E's properties must be valued to prove net assets. My prior view (none) now leans A as the sole choice where facts explicitly leave an owner (GP) unproven as AI. No corrections to NI 45-106 citations noted.}

