PUBLIC RESPONSE: {A}

The NI 45-106 (Ontario, Jan 2021) entity tests require either (i) net assets ≥$5 M on financial statements or (ii) every direct/indirect/beneficial owner of interests themselves being an AI. Individuals meet via the two-year income test (> $200 k solo / > $300 k spousal + expectation), $1 M net-financial-assets test, or $5 M net-assets test.

B, C, D and E each satisfy at least one prong on the explicit facts (spousal-income, spousal net-assets, or entity net-assets ≥$5 M). A fails both entity routes: the LP itself shows no ≥$5 M net assets, and the corporate GP’s AI status is never established after the $6 M gifts (no independent financial statements or closed ownership-chain loop). This structural gap is decisive; no other choice has an equivalent unproven link.

13.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {E}

The entity test under NI 45-106 s. 1.1 (Ontario, Jan 2021) requires either net assets of at least $5 M on the most recent financial statements or that every owner of interests (direct, indirect or beneficial) is itself an accredited investor. In E neither Alex nor Bob meets any individual or spousal threshold on the supplied facts, so the “all owners are AIs” route is unavailable.  

The corporation’s own net-assets position is equally unconfirmed. Only the $5.5 M GIC is quantified; the $300 k liabilities arise from investment properties whose carrying values and fair-market values are never disclosed. Without those figures it is impossible to verify that net assets reach the $5 M threshold on the entity’s financial statements.  

By contrast, A satisfies the “all owners are AIs” route: the three limited partners each clear an individual net-financial-assets or net-assets test, and the GP holding company’s $6 M capitalization (received as cash gifts) places it above the $5 M entity threshold on its own position. B, C and D likewise meet clear income or net-asset prongs on the explicit numbers given. The decisive gaps in E—unquantified real-estate values and non-qualifying owners—therefore keep that corporation outside the accredited-investor definition.}

