B meets the spousal-income test on the combined figures with continued employment. C meets the spousal net-assets test at exactly $5 M. D meets the entity net-assets test after the substantial transfer. A satisfies the “all owners are AIs” route once the three limited partners’ individual qualifications are combined with the GP holding company’s $6 M cash capitalization, which itself meets the entity net-assets threshold.

E fails both routes. Neither Alex nor Bob meets any individual or spousal test on the facts given, so the ownership-chain safe harbour is unavailable. The corporation’s own net-assets position also cannot be confirmed at ≥ $5 M: only the $5.5 M GIC is quantified, while the fair value of the investment properties that generated the $300 k liabilities remains undisclosed. Without that figure the financial-statement test cannot be satisfied. E is therefore the only vehicle that cannot be classified as an accredited investor on the information supplied.}

